    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0433" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/12–2251: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the United States Delegation to
                        the General Assembly</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Roosevelt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-22">December 22,
                        1951</date>.<lb/>[Received December 22—4:22 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Delga 794. Re SC [meeting] membership. Following is text of draft resolution
                    submitted ISC on Dec 19.</p>
                <p>Draft resolution concerning the admission of new members, submitted by the del
                    Union Socialist Republics at the 569th meeting of the Council on 19 December
                    1951:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">“The SC</hi>,</p>
                    <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Having examined</hi> the applications of Albania,
                        the Mongolian People’s Republic, Bulgaria, Romania, Hungary, Finland, Italy,
                        Portugal, Ireland, The Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan, Austria, Ceylon and
                        Nepal for admission to membership of the UN.</p>
                    <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Recommends</hi> the GA to admit those states to
                        membership of the UN.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
